{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "game": "gi",
  "id": "fables-de-fontaine",
  "name": "Fables de Fontaine",
  "sourceUrl": "https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Fables_de_Fontaine",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-08-02T09:05:40.465Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "vol-1",
      "label": "Vol. 1",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The Maiden and the Sun"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-979ee3f5ded30c5a"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The adopted daughter of the fox grew to be of marriageable age, her face as gentle as a beautiful spring."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Delicate and polite was she, and none could name a lady better."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Therefore, the fox said to her daughter,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"My girl, little girl, I am standing in my grave. I may soon no longer be able to care for you as I once did.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Please, choose a husband for yourself. All would be honored to be the one.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-aa2aa5855f347ea3"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The daughter replied,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"If it shall be so, Mother, please have me wed to the most powerful being in this world.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-61155ad89b8dfb2a"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Ah, and that would be the sun,\" the fox said. \"My son-in-law you shall be, O sun shining in the sky.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"No,\" the sun refused. \"These clouds are more powerful, for they block my radiance.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"So it is, then. Flowing clouds, those who block the sun's radiance, please marry my daughter.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Oh, that won't do! The wind blows me away so easily. You're better off entrusting her to the wind!\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-562e894385118f96"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But the wind was stopped by a mountain, and so the fox went to it."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And the mountain demurred, citing conflicts with a mouse."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "That mouse, when enraged, could bore a tunnel through the mountains,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thus, it was mightier by far than the mountains, was it not?"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The mouse suggested the cat, the cat the dog, and the dog, the wolf."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "After having gone through the entire cycle, the Fox found herself facing the sun once more."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "As thus did the young beauty marry the sun."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-3e36a60a2a72ba48"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The story tells the truth that one should accept their destiny, instead of making excuses and trying to evade to the end."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "No matter how honest, or how cunning, one can never escape the duty one ought to shoulder."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-a8ef7bc51b8f3762"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "volumeKey": "vol-2",
      "label": "Vol. 2",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The Crow and the Fox"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-e236b861c4320730"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Once upon a time, a crow perched on a tree, a piece of stolen cheese in its beak."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Seeing the crow, the fox living under the tree looked up and said,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Listen, my friend.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"The thing in your mouth is no enticing feast,\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"But a source of misfortune that anyone sane would avoid like the plague.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Look at your throat and then back at the cheese. Are they matched in size?\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Swallow it, and you might just lose your life.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"The cheesemakers of the city have only let you go,\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Because they know this — or do you think they've handed it to you for safe-keeping?\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-9d6e00ecc36fd250"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The crow cared little for such words, and continued holding onto the cheese."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Seeing that the crow did not intend to give up yet, the fox spoke up once more:"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"My friend,\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"This cheese is not some valuable delicacy!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Think! When you glided between mountain and forest, free of heed or care,\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Did you then hear of something called cheese?\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"If you would listen, I would say that such a thing was never meant for us to enjoy.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Let it rot in the mountains. Let the wind carry it into the sea.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Better that than to let it become a shackle that binds you.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-06751782e9b6d5ea"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The crow fluffed its feathers, but kept its hold on the cheese."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Seeing that the crow still would not give up, the fox sighed."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Come on, my friend,\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"If you truly must savor the taste of cheese,\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"I, a mere fox and bystander, shall not stop you.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"But surely, you must not know how cheese is best consumed.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"If you were to simply swallow it willy-nilly,\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"It would be a terrible waste of such a rare treasure!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Alas, and such a waste it would be, too, of all the recipes I have spent time gleaning from the lands around the world!\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-de378b5b7c749f55"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Suddenly curious, the crow could not help but open its mouth."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"And could you teach me such recipes?\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Even as it did so, the cheese fell to the ground,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And the fox snatched it up, before turning tail and burrowing into its nest."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-12ea3f451389bd18"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This story tells us how those who seek to discover mysteries that they should not know,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Shall lose all, even that which they already had."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-09d9232bf809aee9"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "volumeKey": "vol-3",
      "label": "Vol. 3",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The Tale of the Donkey"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-5dfd645009125c00"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Even when dressed to the nines, a Plain Jane will rarely be mistaken for a socialite."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Everyone in this world has strengths and weaknesses that are theirs and theirs alone."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thus, the only way forward is to know oneself and face one's own flaws."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Don't be like the donkey of this tale, and make an ass of oneself."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-ef8a06c7acb38ca2"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Having learned how the fox seized the cheese, the donkey sought to emulate the crafty fox."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Why is the world like this?\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"The fox is no genius. Why do others always toot her horn?\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Do I, the donkey, not labor every day? Yet, no one cares to even greet me with a smile.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Since this is the case, I shall learn from the fox and do the same as she.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Her little tricks, surely, shall be mine in no time.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-eb311cd70218fb8d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thus, the donkey hid among the trees, and waited for its target to come by."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "As the daughter of the cheesemaker passed by, the donkey bounded over,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And imitating the fox, raised a hoof and said with a smug voice,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Ha! Listen to me! You know nothing about swift travel.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Just throw all your cheese away. Shall your cart not arrive sooner that way?\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-e662b6d9d15feacf"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The young lady was shocked, and she immediately replied,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Oh, you silly donkey! You dare to try to pull my leg?\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Get me my stick! I'm driving this beast back to the mill!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Seeing the stick being waved at it, the donkey ceased speaking at once."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-da5a00de7fc67586"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This tale explains how trying to be someone else and smothering your own identity,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Is by no means beneficial. Indeed, it only leads to more suffering."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-76db1f98afe83382"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
